@Andrzej "masculine, which the moon is in Polish"
I've always found it interesting that in gendered Germanic languages (and at least one Slavic), the moon is masculine and the sun is feminine, whereas in Romance languages, and Greek, it's the other way around. They're all Indo-european languages, and things like that tend to be very conservative. Which is the original? And why did the others change?
Perhaps Sam Lyons or David Connell could shed some, um, light, were they still around.

